cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these data, please cite them as below, together with the associated article (see references)."
type: software
title: "Comparative Variance Partition along the Slow-Fast Continuum"
abstract: >-
  Python code and simulated data that reproduce the results of the article
  "Differential Contributions of Heterogeneity and Stochasticity to
  Individuals' Life Histories along the Slow-fast Continuum". The code
  simulates heterogeneous populations of six synthetic species along the
  slow-fast continuum and partitions the variance in longevity and lifetime
  reproductive output into individual stochasticity and fixed individual
  heterogeneity, including a factorial decomposition among vital rates.
  The data (simulation results, CSV and NumPy formats) are described in the
  README. Python translation of the original MATLAB implementation (v1.0.0).
